{"at":"2026-10-07T04:24:53.245Z","component":"Account Hub submit handler syntax","evidence":["3ab20ed80cb0be874d6d5c3538552120ef041e278df85ede4889bc6bcfa52c2e","537392077e4126ddd0fff3493ea57a73529bd37a2b878af9f8ca311d2594b9ea","55d1100519fa317109466aa9b34a6c92865beb9e77992f8e6bc943626f558539","659fc851c5cb29eca4dfd4145e2403b10675f7ea1283e9d68d98d44b21a4d079","69d784f5d119fcbd01e13d553e1510a8f184aa8980009945b976907a6d8f30fe","6dcada9be973ece64a87a9a027be4d33bff0d0a2e6400d8e501ba1827cf9a18b","88930495679d2fc0f3fe0dd9ba7f77042efef1b0a1414d46ddac11e124e8ed53","9177ceebd3fe92a89c6525bcbaf4e4424d04e7d2cb371899e959335c08ede463","996f00daf3b35bb30a82817cbb1bc3979d0c8e627071781c1696baa23897deec","a318c936f18210394a7688af90eb3b8149f605fb46692e62aa5f433864948fc9","c30c346608178d00b47118eb956b7e03203148088715270e1f14d93c93766ee4","c675592b3df0c9d63a2d213ca1382dd7032e07e340ab42b5e747d220b0369b56","c92d37be2d12e58476c5e8246b191d7e4ce5a8889527cb8672ee7e7f91fdb3f3"],"id":"fc0aa9caec3976454789f21d50a6dc56290bbe3ea4455972375b59317167eee4","kind":"lesson","paths":["mail/components/accountcreation/views/email.mjs","mail/components/accountcreation/templates/accountHubEmailIncomingFormTemplate.inc.xhtml","mail/components/accountcreation/templates/accountHubEmailAutoFormTemplate.inc.xhtml"],"quotes":[{"id":"c675592b3df0c9d63a2d213ca1382dd7032e07e340ab42b5e747d220b0369b56","text":"      case \"submit\":\n        event.preventDefault();\n        if (!event.target.checkValidity()) {\n          return;\n        }\n      // Fall through to handle like forward event.\n      case \"forward\":\n        try {\n          const stateData = this.#currentSubview.captureState?.();\n          await this.#handleForwardAction(this.#currentState, stateData);"},{"id":"659fc851c5cb29eca4dfd4145e2403b10675f7ea1283e9d68d98d44b21a4d079","text":"      </button>\n    </div>\n    <button type=\"submit\" hidden=\"hidden\"></button>\n  </form>\n</html:template>"},{"id":"a318c936f18210394a7688af90eb3b8149f605fb46692e62aa5f433864948fc9","text":"                class=\"animated\"\n                data-l10n-id=\"account-hub-email-label\"\n                data-l10n-attrs=\"accesskey\">\n          </label>\n          <img id=\"emailWarning\"\n              src=\"\"\n              data-l10n-id=\"account-hub-email-warning-icon\"\n              alt=\"\"\n              class=\"form-icon icon-danger input-warning\" />\n          <img id=\"emailSuccess\"\n              src=\"\"\n              alt=\"\"\n              class=\"form-icon icon-success input-success\" />\n          <span id=\"emailErrorMessage\"\n                class=\"input-error-message\"\n                data-l10n-id=\"account-hub-email-error-text\">\n          </span>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <button\n            id=\"manualConfiguration\"\n            class=\"button link-button link-button-sm visibility-hidden\"\n            type=\"button\"\n            data-l10n-id=\"account-hub-email-manual-configuration\"\n          >\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <button type=\"submit\" hidden=\"hidden\"></button>\n  </form>\n</html:template>"}],"repository":"thunderbird","source":{"basis":"Quoted evidence supports the claim; its interpretation still needs current-source checks.","revision":"0b93f0f7a926ed94c8a0646f18b6734ec7cc0f6d","sourceAt":"2026-10-05T22:44:59Z","type":"extraction"},"status":"supported","supersedes":[],"text":"The submit case comments that it falls through to handle the event like forward. The form uses type=submit for the hidden submit action while unrelated actions use type=button. In this controller, keep the fallthrough reason at the switch boundary and name event cases by their actual route. This is a scoped manual syntax recommendation that makes the shared behavior reviewable; it is not a general requirement to use switch fallthrough in event handlers. These conclusions come from static source inspection. No runtime test or accessibility session was run. Full Bugzilla and Phabricator discussion remains pending.","title":"Describe intentional submit fallthrough beside the shared transition","version":1,"visibility":"shared"}
